{"path":"container/unordered_set/begin","title":"std::unordered_set<Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator>::begin, std::unordered_set<Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator>::cbegin","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::unordered_set&lt;Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator&gt;::</span>begin, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::unordered_set&lt;Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator&gt;::</span>cbegin","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/unordered_set/begin","section":"container","kind":"page","summary":"Returns an iterator to the first element of the unordered_set.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">iterator begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">const_iterator begin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">const_iterator cbegin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns an iterator to the first element of the <code>unordered_set</code>.\n</p><p>If the <code>unordered_set</code> is empty, the returned iterator will be equal to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_set/end\">end()</a></span>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-image\">\n<p><img alt=\"range-begin-end.svg\" src=\"/cppreference/images/1/1b/range-begin-end.svg\" width=\"546\" height=\"157\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Iterator to the first element.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Constant.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Because both <code>iterator</code> and <code>const_iterator</code> are constant iterators (and may in fact be the same type), it is not possible to mutate the elements of the container through an iterator returned by any of these member functions.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;unordered_set&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Point <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> x, y<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    Point pts<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>, <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">3</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// points is a set containing the addresses of points</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_set\"><span class=\"kw1297\">std::<span class=\"me2\">unordered_set</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Point<span class=\"sy2\">*</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> points <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span> pts, pts <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, pts <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// Change each y-coordinate of (i, 0) from 0 into i^2 and print the point</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> iter <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> points.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> iter <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> points.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>iter<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>iter<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>y <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>iter<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>iter<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>x<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// iter is a pointer-to-Point*</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"(\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>iter<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>x <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\", \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>iter<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>y <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\") \"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// Now using the range-based for loop, we increase each y-coordinate by 10</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>Point<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> i <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> points<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        i<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>y <span class=\"sy2\">+</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">10</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"(\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> i<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>x <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\", \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> i<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>y <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\") \"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>(3, 9) (1, 1) (2, 4) \n(3, 19) (1, 11) (2, 14)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/unordered_set/end\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>end</span><span>cend</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns an iterator to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/begin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>begin</span><span>cbegin</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx14\">(C++14)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns an iterator to the beginning of a container or array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"container","title":"Containers library"},{"path":"container/unordered_set","title":"std::unordered_set"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::unordered_set<Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator>::begin, std::unordered_set<Key,Hash,KeyEqual,Allocator>::cbegin","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"3 declarations; revisions: since C++11. Returns an iterator to the first element of the unordered_set."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Iterator to the first element."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Constant."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Because both iterator and const_iterator are constant iterators (and may in fact be the same type), it is not possible to mutate the elements of the container…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","